5f-d619-5d2d-aec2-e35257aabcad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275321 #edb/ref 1074 "The coefficient of $(x-1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-2{e}^{-{x}^{2}}+4{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =12x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}-8{x}^{3}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(1),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(1)=12\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{-{1}^{2}}-8\\cdot {1}^{3}\\cdot {e}^{-{1}^{2}}=4{e}^{-1}=\\frac{4}{e}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(1)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot \\frac{4}{e}=\\frac{2}{3e}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x-1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{2}{3e}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05c6bd5e-0a05-54b2-8760-1af815a21d72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1117310d-a59f-5c9e-afac-07ea4e950362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275672 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275672 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275672 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14cad042-e3b8-5970-b4bc-1bab2bf4016f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "181d1c26-e67d-51c2-a26a-430f785d6acb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275702 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275702 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275702 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1837262d-ff49-5dc0-83dc-18a2a52a47d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/re